# Product Requirements Document (PRD)

## Title: `lgtm` — Real-Time Terminal Diff Reviewer & Agent Steering Engine

### 1. Executive Summary & Objective

`lgtm` is a fast terminal-based TUI built in **Rust** designed to run adjacent to coding agents (Claude Code, Aider, OpenHands, custom loops) in multiplexed shells (`tmux`, `Zellij`) or standalone terminal windows.

It transforms diff review from a blocking, manual post-step into a live steering loop:
* Continuous non-blocking diff stream with file-watcher triggers.
* Vim-native modal navigation, instant fuzzy file switching, and file tree drawer.
* One-key context injection (`path:line`) directly into agent input panes.
* Resilient comment re-anchoring across agent iterations.
* Automated heuristic detection for weakened or neutered tests.

---

### 2. User Personas & Target Audience

* **AI-Assisted Engineers:** Developers pairing with CLI agents who need real-time blast-radius visibility without switching out of their terminal workflow.
* **Tech Leads & Reviewers:** Engineers verifying large autonomous refactors and guarding test-suite integrity before commits land.

---

### 3. Core Problems & Solutions

| Problem | Solution in `lgtm` |
| --- | --- |
| **Manual git diff polling & pager lock** | Continuous reactive watcher; sub-millisecond background re-parsing. |
| **Clunky multi-file navigation** | Fuzzy file switcher (`Ctrl-p` / `f`), collapsible file tree (`Tab`), sequential hopping (`]f`/`[f`). |
| **Manual context transcription** | Hitting `Enter` pushes formatted target tokens (`path:line` or code blocks) straight into agent pane. |
| **Comments lost after agent rewrites** | Line-context fuzzy hashing anchors comments across revisions. |
| **Agent test regressions (silently deleted assertions)** | Real-time scanner flags deleted `assert`s, skip decorators, and neutered tests. |
| **External editor disconnect** | One-key jump (`e` / `o`) opens `$EDITOR` at cursor position. |

