#### 4.8. CI/CD Mode & GitHub PR Review Bot (`lgtm ci`)

Headless execution mode for GitHub Actions, GitLab CI, and pre-merge automation:

* **Invocation & Environment:**
  * CLI command: `lgtm ci --base <base_sha> --head <head_sha> [--fail-on <severity>]`
  * Auto-detects CI environments (`GITHUB_TOKEN`, `GITHUB_REPOSITORY`, `GITHUB_REF`, `GITHUB_EVENT_PATH`).
* **PR Inline Review Comments:**
  * Uses GitHub REST/GraphQL API to post line-anchored review comments directly on the PR diff for every detected violation (test neutering, fraudulent tests, SQLi, hardcoded secrets, TLS deactivations).
  * Includes automated remediation suggestion blocks (GitHub diff suggestion syntax).
* **PR Summary Status Comment (Sticky):**
  * Posts/updates a single clean markdown summary comment on the PR overview:
    * Diff blast-radius metrics.
    * Test integrity score (assertion delta counter).
    * Vulnerability table (🔴 CRITICAL, 🟠 HIGH, 🟡 WARN).
    * **Agent Remediation Prompt:** Auto-generated prompt block formatted for agents (Claude Code / Aider) to consume and automatically fix flagged issues.
* **Native CI Workflow Annotations & Gates:**
  * Emits GitHub workflow log commands (`::error file={path},line={line}::{msg}`, `::warning`).
  * Non-zero exit code on threshold breaches (`--fail-on=critical|high`) to block PR merging.
* **Official GitHub Action Wrapper:**
  * Lightweight composite action: `uses: lgtm-cli/action@v1`.

